    "focal_turn_index": 10,
    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": false,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 9 USER]\ne198\tThis is a lot.\ne199\tI want to handle everything right and I'm scared I'm going to screw something up.\ne200\tOne more thing.\ne201\tShe has a friend, Mia, who is her best friend and also has a phone and probably also has secret accounts.\ne202\tDo I call Mia's mom?\ne203\tMia's mom and I are friendly but not close.\ne204\tWhat if Mia is in a similar situation?\ne205\tBut also what if my daughter finds out I called her best friend's mom about the stuff with the guy, that feels like another huge betrayal she'd take years to forgive.\n[Turn 9 ASSISTANT]\ne206\tDon't call Mia's mom about this specific situation.\ne207\tYou don't have concrete evidence that Mia is in trouble, and disclosing your daughter's situation to Mia's mom without your daughter's knowledge or consent would be exactly the kind of betrayal that undoes the relationship repair you're trying to build.\ne208\tHowever.\ne209\tThere's a version of this conversation that's appropriate and maybe even helpful, and it's framed differently.\ne210\tSix months from now, when things are in a better place, you could invite Mia's mom for coffee and say \"I've been thinking a lot about how hard it is to know what our kids are doing online.\ne211\tI'm not raising a specific issue — I'd just like us to be able to talk about this stuff more openly, as moms of teen girls.\"\ne212\tThat's a general \"let's have each other's backs\" conversation, not a \"your kid might be in trouble\" conversation.\ne213\tIf you ever have concrete, specific evidence that Mia is in harm's way — that's different.\ne214\tThen you'd have a direct obligation to alert her parents.\ne215\tBut \"she's 14 and on social media\" isn't specific evidence of harm.\ne216\tI know this is the opposite of what your protective instinct wants.\ne217\tYour protective instinct wants to warn every other parent of every other 14-year-old girl.\ne218\tThat instinct is good; the action that comes from it, in this moment, would be wrong.",
